new file mode 100644
index 0000000..292bceb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/self-hosting.md
@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@
+# Self-hosting Fizzy
+
+Fizzy is designed to run on a single Linux server with Docker. The included
+[Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org/) configuration deploys the whole app as one
+container:
+
+- SQLite stores the database, the cache, the job queue, and Action Cable data.
+- Uploaded files are stored on disk.
+- Background jobs (Solid Queue) run inside the web container.
+- [kamal-proxy](https://github.com/basecamp/kamal-proxy) terminates TLS and
+  gets a free Let's Encrypt certificate for your hostname.
+
+Everything is kept in a Docker volume, so your data survives the next deploy.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- A Linux server with Docker installed, reachable over SSH. Kamal installs
+  Docker for you if it isn't there.
+- A domain (or subdomain) whose DNS `A`/`AAAA` record points at the server.
+  Ports `80` and `443` must be open to the internet so Let's Encrypt can issue a
+  certificate.
+- An SMTP server Fizzy can send email through. Fizzy uses email for magic-link
+  sign in, so this is required for anyone to log in.
+- Ruby and the project's gems installed on the machine you deploy from (see the
+  [development guide](development.md)).
+
+## 1. Fork and clone the repository
+
+Fork the repository on GitHub, then clone your fork:
+
+```sh
+git clone https://github.com/<your-user>/fizzy.git
+cd fizzy
+```
+
+## 2. Configure the deployment
+
+Edit `config/deploy.yml` and fill in every value marked `TODO`:
+
+- `servers.web` — the SSH hostname or IP address of your server.
+- `proxy.host` and `env.clear.APP_FQDN` — the hostname you'll serve Fizzy from.
+  They must both be the same hostname (e.g. `fizzy.example.com`).
+- `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` — the `From` address Fizzy should use for email.
+- `SMTP_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_PORT`, and `SMTP_USERNAME` — your mail server details.
+
+If you're deploying to an ARM server, change `builder.arch` to `arm64`.
+
+## 3. Add your secrets
+
+Kamal reads secrets from `.kamal/secrets`. Provide these in your environment
+before running Kamal (or replace the `$VARIABLE` references with the values
+directly if the repository is private):
+
+- `SECRET_KEY_BASE` — a stable Rails secret. Generate one once and keep it:
+
+  ```sh
+  export SECRET_KEY_BASE=$(bin/rails secret)
+  ```
+
+  Don't regenerate it on every deploy: changing it invalidates existing
+  sessions and signed cookies.
+
+- `SMTP_PASSWORD` — the password for your mail server, if it requires one:
+
+  ```sh
+  export SMTP_PASSWORD=...
+  ```
+
+If you use `bin/rails credentials:edit` for other secrets, export
+`RAILS_MASTER_KEY` as well; `.kamal/secrets` already passes it through.
+
+## 4. Deploy
+
+From the repository root, run:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+Kamal installs Docker and kamal-proxy on the server if needed, builds the image,
+ships it to the server through a local registry forwarded over SSH, boots the
+container, and requests a certificate for your hostname. When it finishes, open
+https://your-hostname and sign up.
+
+Subsequent deploys only need:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+## Data persistence
+
+`config/deploy.yml` mounts the `fizzy_storage` Docker volume at
+`/rails/storage`. That directory holds the SQLite databases and uploaded files,
+and because it's a volume it is not touched by a deploy. Migrations run
+automatically when a new container boots.
+
+To back everything up, copy that volume off the server periodically, for
+example:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm -v fizzy_storage:/data -v "$PWD":/backup alpine \
+  tar czf /backup/fizzy-storage.tar.gz -C /data .
+```
+
+## Operational commands
+
+Kamal aliases are defined in `config/deploy.yml`; the useful ones are:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal console   # Rails console
+bin/kamal shell     # shell in the container
+bin/kamal logs -f   # tail the app logs
+bin/kamal dbc       # SQLite console
+```
+
+## Optional extras
+
+- **Web push notifications.** Generate VAPID keys and set `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY`
+  and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` in the deploy `env`. See the
+  [development guide](development.md#web-push-notifications).
+- **MySQL.** Set `DATABASE_ADAPTER=mysql` and the relevant `MYSQL_*` variables,
+  and add a MySQL accessory. See `config/database.mysql.yml`.
+- **S3 storage.** Set `ACTIVE_STORAGE_SERVICE=s3` and the `S3_*` variables. See
+  `config/storage.oss.yml`.
